refactor(App): standardize structure and add user session identity

Reorganize src/ into the layered controllers/services/models/features
layout (config + core), and promote user identity to a first-class
concept: sessions are now scoped per room+user with a clean User model
(id + displayName), Ami greets by name on a fresh conversation, and
/status reports who she is talking to. Idle sessions post a farewell
back into the room via a pluggable SessionStore expiry callback.

Verified live on the ts.net instance: new session created and greeting
by name ("Hi admin! 👋"); /status returns "Talking to **admin** (admin)
in room **Ami Help Desk**".

Assisted-by: opencode:hy3-free
